        "procedure": "H-tritox was prepared from diethyl carbonate (6.18 mL) in diethyl ether (50 mL) added over 2 h to tert-butyllithium (90 mL, 1.7 M in pentane), then hydrolyzed at 0 °C with water (50 mL) and acetic acid (10 mL), washed, dried, and sublimed at 80 °C. A solution of H-tritox (4.9 mmol) in hexane (20 mL) was dropped into [Tb{N(SiMe3)2}3] (1.6 mmol) in hexane (50 mL) and stirred at room temperature for 24 h. After condensation the product was dissolved in hexane/THF (5 mL/2 mL) and cooled to −20 °C, giving colourless crystals of 2.",
